    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang** (75.04) and **Corbin Carroll** (71.43) emerge as the clear anchors of our offensive production. **Brice Turang** is a priority start, buoyed by a significant park factor (+14%) and the opportunistic combination of a slow opposing delivery, which maximizes his elite sprint speed for stolen base potential. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong lineup position and a favorable platoon advantage against Cavalli. While **Jose Caballero** (63.66) finds himself in the bottom third of the order, his utility cannot be overlooked; a 13% boost from his dynamic platoon splits against Suarez, combined with favorable wind conditions, makes him a high-efficiency asset for our pursuit of SB and R.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, who logged a respectable 42.79 efficiency score but fell just short of our threshold. Despite his pedigree, **Austin Riley** was sidelined in favor of **Kyle Karros**, who secured the 3B spot thanks to a massive park-factor boost that offset a challenging matchup against an elite arm. We remain cautious regarding **Travis Bazzana** (42.86), whose score is heavily suppressed by a brutal matchup against deGrom; he remains in the lineup only for his lead-off role and the necessity of maintaining our daily game caps. Finally, we continue to monitor **Mickey Moniak**, who remains unavailable on the IL, while the rest of our depth\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Dalton Rushing**\u2014is slated to contribute as marginal but necessary cogs in our 5x5 rotation.",
